#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054802 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054499 :question/id #uuid "2efe9f75-18c0-5a86-b56b-3f338b7e5c2d" :question/math-academy-id "e-1702" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the graph of the straight line below?\n\nI. $y=2x-1$\n\nII. $y=\\dfrac{1}{2}x-1$\n\nIII. $2x-y=1$\n\n![](images/93/93dc9d447c15e4597549996b1f0b533cf86783b5cc5df032a4c46d4ca8934abc.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, we can choose $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,-1)$ and $(2,3)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/a9/a9f18453dedb1763908825301f80ef86307d3a3aceaf678bbe8579a42a0996f5.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation I: $y=2x-1.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-1)$ and $B(2,3),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1) & =2(0)-1 \\\\ -1 & =-1\\,✓ \\\\ (3) & =2(2)-1 \\\\ 3 & =3\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=2x-1$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation II: $y=\\dfrac{1}{2}x-1.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-1)$ and $B(2,3),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1) & =\\frac{1}{2}(0)-1 \\\\ -1 & =-1\\,✓ \\\\ (3) & =\\frac{1}{2}(2)-1 \\\\ 3 & =0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=\\dfrac{1}{2}x-1$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation III: $2x-y=1.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-1)$ and $B(2,3),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(0)-(-1) & =1 \\\\ 1 & =1\\,✓ \\\\ 2(2)-(3) & =1 \\\\ 1 & =1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $2x-y=1$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\nOf the given equations, the only equations that represented the line in the graph were $y=2x-1$ and $2x-y=1,$ corresponding to answer choices I and III. Therefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3986a3cd-c543-54e9-8d55-f744d9436313" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055368 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "edec9d12-0bd4-51b1-857c-39b0d3a639e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439845} {:answer/id #uuid "ba4130b8-9669-55b8-8101-3fcb6c6ada16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439846}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "edec9d12-0bd4-51b1-857c-39b0d3a639e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439845} :answer-field/id #uuid "69a5e73f-3177-5c10-a5a9-440d3c78400f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440280} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9cb663d8-de5a-51e3-bb4d-8e4f975e7db1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439847} {:answer/id #uuid "1f0202b1-3256-56a6-9f81-b5d0622b9978" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439848}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f0202b1-3256-56a6-9f81-b5d0622b9978" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439848} :answer-field/id #uuid "49e99a0a-f180-5be2-8fc7-1134f81777c9" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440281} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27364161-b9ad-5a6e-b527-4b3e2d5b8883" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439849} {:answer/id #uuid "d9e1b9e7-60c6-56f9-aca1-3d50f7fe497b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439850}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27364161-b9ad-5a6e-b527-4b3e2d5b8883" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439849} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8ff5166-67c3-5684-8f52-2c346e801f1d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440282}] :question/id #uuid "56e71e28-d3a5-545f-bf8d-30361fbf20ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-54285" :question/problem "![](images/4c/4ce176ba6bb73da8d6af410bedad4733cf3e705c70e28f133d771b89f78130c5.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $y = x + \\frac{1}{2}$\n- **II.** $y = \\frac{1}{2}x + 2$\n- **III.** $y = \\frac{1}{2}x + \\frac{1}{2}$" :question/worked-solution "The line crosses the y-axis at 2 and passes through (4,4); its slope is 1/2. Therefore y=x/2+2, statement II."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055431 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "acf10a5d-ded4-5b84-b33b-6fd30a508b8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439851} {:answer/id #uuid "136aebe2-1e23-5e43-bca6-1706231d0c1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439852}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "acf10a5d-ded4-5b84-b33b-6fd30a508b8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439851} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bfae510-b96d-5e86-9727-d50c4fd631a3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440283} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c172c4a-e1a8-56f7-9795-82510cd46049" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439853} {:answer/id #uuid "aa1a8025-4883-5f71-a62a-efae12144e11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c172c4a-e1a8-56f7-9795-82510cd46049" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439853} :answer-field/id #uuid "aeab6991-adc5-5ace-ba4f-ecc5f05657e8" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440284} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6aba6425-8dab-5304-9842-8e92e1722604" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439855} {:answer/id #uuid "48a91d43-b10e-5fa5-ac58-14ddb60ffc8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439856}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48a91d43-b10e-5fa5-ac58-14ddb60ffc8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439856} :answer-field/id #uuid "415c96ce-c78f-50f0-9f80-e3fc5b279dba" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440285}] :question/id #uuid "2fe51fc5-fce7-5fb6-911c-f561e72ff3fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-59732" :question/problem "![](images/4d/4d78eaaedd26a27d9163fdcddfce5c5ed429e441a75d361f0840935fce9235c6.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x + 2y = 4$\n- **II.** $y = 2 - x$\n- **III.** $y = 4 - x$" :question/worked-solution "The line has intercepts (0,4) and (4,0), so its equation is y=4-x, statement III."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490279 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ce4d23e-eb28-56bb-bb93-3733846a6e64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489585} {:answer/id #uuid "59fbb6ed-802e-5fc7-981b-ad071fe8f05d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489735} {:answer/id #uuid "ad32efea-57f2-50ab-8978-d4988074759d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489894} {:answer/id #uuid "c0d8e2ce-cf6e-51e6-a3d1-b415eae5cfb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489933} {:answer/id #uuid "e108ba0b-b8a5-543a-a12b-2f22efb52a6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad32efea-57f2-50ab-8978-d4988074759d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489894} :answer-field/id #uuid "8571c77b-dc56-5521-b8ff-cf319f34e7c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490152}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9d3bda62-1eef-5cb9-886b-004877c9a204" :question/math-academy-id "q-71837" :question/problem "![](images/f8/f886e9f5dfef693d1ea5d5a0a907a886be368549c1b9a4d43dce257d070e2fa2.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nI. $y+3x=6$\n\nII. $\\frac{1}{3}y+x=2$\n\nIII. $y=-3x+6$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,6)$ and $(2,0)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/d6/d6cb6d026c181d79bda5c809729eb070c554c2025a287577df0330d1dd8a03e7.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation I: $y+3x=6.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,6)$ and $B(2,0)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6)+3(0) & =6 \\\\ 6 & =6\\,✓ \\\\ (0)+3(2) & =6 \\\\ 6 & =6\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y+3x=6$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation II: $\\frac{1}{3}y+x=2.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,6)$ and $B(2,0)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}(6)+(0) & =2 \\\\ 2+0 & =2 \\\\ 2 & =2\\,✓ \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}(0)+(2) & =2 \\\\ 0+2 & =2 \\\\ 2 & =2\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,$\\frac{1}{3}y+x=2$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation III: $y=-3x+6.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,6)$ and $B(2,0)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6) & =-3(0)+6 \\\\ 6 & =6\\,✓ \\\\ (0) & =-3(2)+6 \\\\ 0 & =-6+6 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=-3x+6$ is  an equation of the line in the graph.\n\nAll the given equations represented the line in the graph. Therefore, the correct answer is \"I, II and III.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490287 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "026cf452-bbce-5666-b06e-eea33f9d7832" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489517} {:answer/id #uuid "9acb1b55-d961-5760-970a-55e90ab17c7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489858} {:answer/id #uuid "c834e69d-11f0-589f-aef2-acdc449ab184" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489948} {:answer/id #uuid "c9f1f968-d792-57b5-9f02-cbac084ac726" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489956} {:answer/id #uuid "e524c8b2-8988-581d-b06e-10a171578329" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490013}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "026cf452-bbce-5666-b06e-eea33f9d7832" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489517} :answer-field/id #uuid "44f33cfa-5885-5a2f-90fc-d69e3d361204" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490113}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a635937b-674b-54dd-a770-48fe7b870be8" :question/math-academy-id "q-54293" :question/problem "![](images/71/716836dd3dfc93ac26bf9a960d5edcd04da96907b98c39e926a917b7b8feeeee.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nI. $y=-2x+\\frac{1}{2}$\n\nII. $y=-\\frac{1}{2}x+2$\n\nIII. $y=\\frac{1}{2}x+2$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,2)$ and $(4,0)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/2b/2b9174d86d123228ae24fffeda4d2e4741e4a776f6671f7eff38340a59ba4d40.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation I: $y=-2x+\\frac{1}{2}.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,2)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2) & =-1(0)+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=-2x+\\frac{1}{2}$ is *not* equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation II: $y=-\\frac{1}{2}x+2.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,2)$ and $B(4,0)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2) & =-\\frac{1}{2}(0)+2 \\\\ 2 & =2\\,✓ \\\\ (0) & =-\\frac{1}{2}(4)+2 \\\\ 0 & =-2+2 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,$y=-\\frac{1}{2}x+2$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation III: $y=\\frac{1}{2}x+2.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,2)$ and $B(4,0)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2) & =\\frac{1}{2}(0)+2 \\\\ 2 & =2\\,✓ \\\\ (0) & =\\frac{1}{2}(4)+2 \\\\ 0 & =2+2 \\\\ 0 & =4\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=\\frac{1}{2}x+2$ is *not* equation of the line in the graph.\n\nOf the given equations, the only equation that represented the line in the graph was $y=-\\frac{1}{2}x+2,$ corresponding to answer choice II. Therefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501323 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c3da477-2f8c-5b2b-8534-55a21ba63377" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501316} {:answer/id #uuid "25f25fe2-2d7e-54ee-967f-6bb9248a110b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501319} {:answer/id #uuid "277c7b29-7430-521f-9d76-62c8fd5674b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501320} {:answer/id #uuid "92cee00b-fc75-54a9-b753-d48fe2943e17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501325} {:answer/id #uuid "bae18ee6-b3b9-5327-ad96-6d55d7e27bdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501330}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c3da477-2f8c-5b2b-8534-55a21ba63377" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501316} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1108d84-a4e2-5397-a2f7-9adbc9f6a9b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501332}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "61c31858-4aad-578b-a21e-e968c5ca8b40" :question/problem "![](images/76/7688f7536a66b7a737d58031b9b8752aabaa84a914ff5deb799e7060d7a90aeb.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nI. $y=-4x+\\frac{2}{3}$\n\nII. $y=-\\frac{2}{3}x+4$\n\nIII. $y=\\frac{2}{3}x+4$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,4)$ and $(6,0)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/cb/cbec3e69d5f8a5bbcfc7d97d95c9f3d3ec93be63b1c8de2ceba3e3a24a9dba13.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation I: $y=-4x+\\frac{2}{3}.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,4)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4) & =-4(0)+\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 4 & =\\frac{2}{3}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=-4x+\\frac{2}{3}$ is *not* equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation II: $y=-\\frac{2}{3}x+4.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,4)$ and $B(6,0)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4) & =-\\frac{2}{3}(0)+4 \\\\ 4 & =4\\,✓ \\\\ (0) & =-\\frac{2}{3}(6)+4 \\\\ 0 & =-4+4 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,$y=-\\frac{2}{3}x+4$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation III: $y=\\frac{2}{3}x+4.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,4)$ and $B(6,0)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4) & =\\frac{2}{3}(0)+4 \\\\ 4 & =4\\,✓ \\\\ (0) & =\\frac{2}{3}(6)+4 \\\\ 0 & =4+4 \\\\ 0 & =8\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=\\frac{2}{3}x+4$ is *not* equation of the line in the graph.\n\nOf the given equations, the only equation that represented the line in the graph was $y=-\\frac{2}{3}x+4,$ corresponding to answer choice II. Therefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501329 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "015abcb0-80a5-5dc1-b79f-79d7198d8b47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501315} {:answer/id #uuid "1d75fe37-e4ce-5bc4-98f8-d2fb16b56012" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501318} {:answer/id #uuid "7d397adc-2e01-5cd8-a945-f4855a2fd4b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501324} {:answer/id #uuid "9b3194ba-e75e-59ea-b78e-7f3fe9b442f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501327} {:answer/id #uuid "e6c58012-7269-5610-aef9-dbc7d838d8f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6c58012-7269-5610-aef9-dbc7d838d8f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501333} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1a010cc-cba0-5af2-91cb-dae10509e3db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501334}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b3d6f732-ed9f-51fe-87bd-f9f387742c79" :question/problem "![](images/87/87cbbd5a53079bb2cd744e1af18e901f6e54239a0fc6330984659c75cbdd3509.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nI. $y+3x=9$\n\nII. $\\frac{1}{3}y+x=3$\n\nIII. $y=-3x+9$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,9)$ and $(3,0)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/c3/c3a0113d32377bd9bac1569081dce1caad04e1cd385805fbb225c3964e7f85d7.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation I: $y+3x=9.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,9)$ and $B(3,0)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(9)+3(0) & =9 \\\\ 9 & =9\\,✓ \\\\ (0)+3(3) & =9 \\\\ 9 & =9\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y+3x=9$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation II: $\\frac{1}{3}y+x=3.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,9)$ and $B(3,0)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}(9)+(0) & =3 \\\\ 3+0 & =3 \\\\ 3 & =3\\,✓ \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}(0)+(3) & =3 \\\\ 0+3 & =3 \\\\ 3 & =3\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,$\\frac{1}{3}y+x=3$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation III: $y=-3x+9.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,9)$ and $B(3,0)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(9) & =-3(0)+9 \\\\ 9 & =9\\,✓ \\\\ (0) & =-3(3)+9 \\\\ 0 & =-9+9 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=-3x+9$ is  an equation of the line in the graph.\n\nAll the given equations represented the line in the graph. Therefore, the correct answer is \"I, II and III.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501335 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "116550ec-7c28-5e18-9fdd-f2d1f181ab88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501317} {:answer/id #uuid "4566a58e-dd27-57f2-8c17-67e13d84f401" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501321} {:answer/id #uuid "9a9607e4-f2bb-5686-8bd2-b386551546bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501326} {:answer/id #uuid "a8e72227-20c4-5321-a16a-1705dfdcf169" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501328} {:answer/id #uuid "cf447eac-1836-54a3-8082-5758760bcbed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501331}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf447eac-1836-54a3-8082-5758760bcbed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501331} :answer-field/id #uuid "5912bad9-fd12-5d7e-8bfc-20dae374c49f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501322}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ff7154d8-1178-59c1-89cf-d6727039f41b" :question/problem "![](images/f0/f0218ba02ef7305b1f22582379d15e8da24c859a239b45130c053aa5c3f8cde1.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nI. $y=-3x+\\frac{3}{8}$\n\nII. $y=-\\frac{3}{8}x+3$\n\nIII. $y=\\frac{3}{8}x+3$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,3)$ and $(8,0)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/f1/f193f5ea70aa459427c5c4abecfdb74c3e12c6de4e22522d71f5ca1f6b1b9cc1.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation I: $y=-3x+\\frac{3}{8}.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,3)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3) & =-3(0)+\\frac{3}{8} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{3}{8}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=-3x+\\frac{3}{8}$ is *not* equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation II: $y=-\\frac{3}{8}x+3.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,3)$ and $B(8,0)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3) & =-\\frac{3}{8}(0)+3 \\\\ 3 & =3\\,✓ \\\\ (0) & =-\\frac{3}{8}(8)+3 \\\\ 0 & =-3+3 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,$y=-\\frac{3}{8}x+3$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation III: $y=\\frac{3}{8}x+3.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,3)$ and $B(8,0)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3) & =\\frac{3}{8}(0)+3 \\\\ 3 & =3\\,✓ \\\\ (0) & =\\frac{3}{8}(8)+3 \\\\ 0 & =3+3 \\\\ 0 & =6\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=\\frac{3}{8}x+3$ is *not* equation of the line in the graph.\n\nOf the given equations, the only equation that represented the line in the graph was $y=-\\frac{3}{8}x+3,$ corresponding to answer choice II. Therefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Line Given a Graph"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059714 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059527 :question/id #uuid "e2b211fe-d37a-55dd-bf76-9ffab2b6f128" :question/math-academy-id "e-4297" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle -4, 6 \\rangle$. Find $\\mid \\,\\mathbf{a}\\, \\mid$." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid a \\mid &= \\sqrt{a_{x}^{2} + a_{y}^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(-4)^{2} + (6)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{16 + 36} \\\\\n&= 2\\sqrt{13}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6b4ebe4-9baa-5ff0-847a-49d99ba69795" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048882 :topic/math-academy-id 1101 :topic/title "The Magnitude of a Vector"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060029 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "867aed2c-b35e-5007-9ac2-00eb9f789e80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056533} {:answer/id #uuid "b570b441-3e76-5296-a70a-898635c0d51b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056534} {:answer/id #uuid "1e5efcaa-fda8-5f46-86a8-ec26f06edd9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056535} {:answer/id #uuid "2fd699d3-7d66-5b5d-9684-70191f970035" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056536} {:answer/id #uuid "56b171f0-eae2-5de6-86da-e18b78da9838" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056537}] :answer-field/id #uuid "0c808bac-3136-50e9-88db-5847268bcea6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056532}] :question/id #uuid "f764385e-ba4e-56aa-912a-4bdb3a698813" :question/math-academy-id "q-1325" :question/problem "If $v = ⟨4,-1⟩$, then what is the magnitude of $v$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060126 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a79d21fc-302a-5450-a54f-6475533b9ce7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{19}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057115} {:answer/id #uuid "e2de1a7d-f3cd-583a-9023-113e1389cccb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{152}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057116} {:answer/id #uuid "f12252ac-d673-5896-9285-85965a7929b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057117} {:answer/id #uuid "22c4967f-8145-57dd-b805-7191087f6156" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057118} {:answer/id #uuid "3cab3961-9873-5028-99db-92118b7dacac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{157}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057119}] :answer-field/id #uuid "c8bc4442-f564-5392-8824-4c50f5f84d3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057114}] :question/id #uuid "9ada1995-eb39-5223-994f-7ad65f7c8096" :question/math-academy-id "q-18046" :question/problem "Let $a = ⟨ - 12, 3⟩$. Find $\\mid a \\mid$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233594 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b8c6e450-fe10-5923-accc-8b824e3c81c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-18047" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨5,9⟩.$ Find $|\\,a\\,|.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\,| & =\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(5)^{2}+(9)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+81} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{106}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233595 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "26fce79e-92f6-594d-aec2-af45c6145c5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-18048" :question/problem "if $a=⟨-4,8⟩$, then  what is the magnitude of  $a?$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\,| & =\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(8)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{80} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16\\cdot 5} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501352 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "079b9a79-06f2-5db8-b532-db1a9740e2a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501340} {:answer/id #uuid "16cda31a-522e-5e9a-a392-a12fa93be895" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7 \\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501345} {:answer/id #uuid "3526a895-cf9a-5109-8227-ed027b72f819" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501350} {:answer/id #uuid "6a1ef581-8afe-5794-950b-84a12f504046" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7 \\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501355} {:answer/id #uuid "d22787e2-9989-5b78-8574-2c6529783d81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16cda31a-522e-5e9a-a392-a12fa93be895" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7 \\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501345} :answer-field/id #uuid "23498b7a-da4b-56a7-9c98-4f68c00e1b13" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501348}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "41ade605-a594-51dc-a5e5-aa2a79dd3288" :question/problem "If $v = ⟨28,-7⟩$, then what is the magnitude of $v$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid v \\mid &= \\sqrt{v_{x}^{2} + v_{y}^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(28)^{2} + (-7)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{784 + 49} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{833} \\\\\n&= 7 \\sqrt{17}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501357 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c640eee-d856-5312-8771-dad05b7c6762" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{157}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501342} {:answer/id #uuid "821c68ef-2b90-5fc8-a59c-0b8635be19d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\sqrt{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501358} {:answer/id #uuid "c4f22dab-ab01-58f3-9151-c04ebd74818d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501367} {:answer/id #uuid "d83c1ede-114e-527e-9711-2a5a0994572a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\sqrt{19}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501371} {:answer/id #uuid "ef0303eb-1361-5a96-bc1b-e6932e54f7cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 \\sqrt{38}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4f22dab-ab01-58f3-9151-c04ebd74818d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501367} :answer-field/id #uuid "457a7096-8d37-50cb-8701-94bd45550806" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501353}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "816d7973-cac7-5db1-9b8c-ad0a12ecb372" :question/problem "Let $a = ⟨-24,6⟩$. Find $\\mid a \\mid$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid a \\mid &= \\sqrt{a_{x}^{2} + a_{y}^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(-24)^{2} + (6)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{576 + 36} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{612} \\\\\n&= 6 \\sqrt{17}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501363 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1166a049-ffe2-5e3a-870c-263a0d75bacc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501344} {:answer/id #uuid "28bccbcc-bd8f-5706-b854-b22cee7197aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501349} {:answer/id #uuid "8b31f907-8674-5200-b063-1e2baada7b51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 \\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501359} {:answer/id #uuid "97b53586-7d07-5f4a-8f6d-d1d819591895" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 \\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501361} {:answer/id #uuid "ca0b084d-35e0-5396-b518-e1026823c088" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501369}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b31f907-8674-5200-b063-1e2baada7b51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 \\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501359} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e7f07d7-dafc-52e1-b433-b07086c6938b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501347}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "adf1662e-c80f-5fd1-b06c-e22ab1eebd14" :question/problem "If $v = ⟨20,-5⟩$, then what is the magnitude of $v$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid v \\mid &= \\sqrt{v_{x}^{2} + v_{y}^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(20)^{2} + (-5)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{400 + 25} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{425} \\\\\n&= 5 \\sqrt{17}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501365 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c3d8879-93de-55cc-be7c-4a7fdd7caa41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501341} {:answer/id #uuid "1b0c96f0-4141-5071-82ec-9a318142c503" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501346} {:answer/id #uuid "76190476-73bf-5a12-a0a3-308cd863c503" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501356} {:answer/id #uuid "916bd653-ebb2-5ee6-9f35-2355af64e70e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501360} {:answer/id #uuid "b7ed0201-83ce-52ad-ab56-02aadbb147ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501366}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b0c96f0-4141-5071-82ec-9a318142c503" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501346} :answer-field/id #uuid "044be5b2-95d6-51b9-9be7-aeb276e4b949" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501339}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b30d0f8c-c583-56ee-9c61-e481453474bb" :question/problem "If $v = ⟨8,-2⟩$, then what is the magnitude of $v$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid v \\mid &= \\sqrt{v_{x}^{2} + v_{y}^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(8)^{2} + (-2)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{64 + 4} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{68} \\\\\n&= 2 \\sqrt{17}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501373 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10d69312-e1f8-5ede-927a-bb12c1a4bdac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 \\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501343} {:answer/id #uuid "552951ba-838c-563a-a702-f44f6524104a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 \\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501354} {:answer/id #uuid "a8eaa732-503b-5d3e-9400-adc2a8028bcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501362} {:answer/id #uuid "afe02226-de3c-552f-bc03-c7afecf61b45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501364} {:answer/id #uuid "c91c20b6-0c18-5ae8-ba08-4ddadb442e99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "552951ba-838c-563a-a702-f44f6524104a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 \\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501354} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bd46d81-0236-582b-868f-f4e59aa85b3d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501351}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f0caf898-ce5d-5506-b145-31d60aeb15df" :question/problem "If $v = ⟨16,-4⟩$, then what is the magnitude of $v$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid v \\mid &= \\sqrt{v_{x}^{2} + v_{y}^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(16)^{2} + (-4)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{256 + 16} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{272} \\\\\n&= 4 \\sqrt{17}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Magnitude of a Vector Given in Component Form"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059715 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059528 :question/id #uuid "d4ad6011-24a4-5642-997f-dcc4e807224f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4298" :question/problem "Let $A(1,3)$ and $B(2,-2)$. Find $\\mid \\overrightarrow{AB} \\mid$.\n\n![](images/f9/f95ee3c5c81750d97019d910350e4c78f0962baa682c834928450a451691145a.png)" :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\nOA^(→) = a = i + 3j,; OB^(→) = b = 2i - 2j\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB^(→) &= OB^(→) - OA^(→) \\\\\n&= b - a \\\\\n&= (2i - 2j) - (i + 3j) \\\\\n&= i - 5j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid AB^(→) \\mid &= \\sqrt{1^{2} + (-5)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{1 + 25} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{26}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bc170fa-a70e-55af-8f3e-f4ea07431e30" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050136 :topic/math-academy-id 244 :topic/title "Addition and Scalar Multiplication of Cartesian Vectors in 2D"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060127 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fa76cd1-659d-5a5b-8d30-aa37db4db6b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057121} {:answer/id #uuid "c207c803-b1ce-5924-b942-d55d34b0a896" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057122} {:answer/id #uuid "fb4bdbac-dae8-512d-9f28-a6d1ca641844" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057123} {:answer/id #uuid "5c31b652-4b6c-5d88-8099-aa3b8dbea173" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057124} {:answer/id #uuid "70729c42-11e6-5309-82bb-19226d272451" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057125}] :answer-field/id #uuid "21f89363-a985-51cc-946e-14f2aa27f506" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057120}] :question/id #uuid "6a56ae9f-24f2-57fe-8fdd-fdcdaeb8e97e" :question/math-academy-id "q-18051" :question/problem "![](images/2c/2c1f9580f07d06af7ec900ee63c95872e06f459107e64cf1b5117d928efdab22.png)\n\nLet $A(-4, 1)$ and $B(3, 0)$. Find $\\mid AB^(→) \\mid$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060128 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "859a4033-c7be-5ff5-af88-1823e959391b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057127} {:answer/id #uuid "ad6482c5-d423-5cfa-b5c4-60571c0a06c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{23}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057128} {:answer/id #uuid "e1496379-7a78-53b1-8d89-c51305772b95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057129} {:answer/id #uuid "e7ded905-451e-5e8d-87f6-0bff47652269" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057130} {:answer/id #uuid "4818a873-c410-58c3-9fa9-c071285aa2cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057131}] :answer-field/id #uuid "60525c6f-c622-5ce0-b076-32a8f28ba4a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057126}] :question/id #uuid "1c261405-1fb7-5f8f-992e-8a8c19696484" :question/math-academy-id "q-18052" :question/problem "![](images/0d/0d92a4d7b9c59b0d6bc8ffec9926bcf189c9bbe808c5bed7a02d6ab09bcebcd0.png)\n\nLet $P(-2, 2)$ and $Q(3, 3)$. Find $\\mid PQ^(→) \\mid$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233366 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "02dcce11-c60f-5753-ba12-d8ce046f2ae1" :question/math-academy-id "q-125118" :question/problem "![](images/f3/f35a3ad730621023ec86e5727588fc86083ee500b3a72c55ab2808bd290019e9.png)\n\nLet $P(1,2)$ and $Q(-2,1).$ Find $|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}|.$" :question/worked-solution "We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OP}=p=i+2j, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OQ}=q=-2i+j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =q-p \\\\  & =(-2i+j)-(i+2j) \\\\  & =-3i-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233596 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f6f7008d-b645-50b0-a00b-9cf227ed2ff3" :question/math-academy-id "q-18049" :question/problem "![](images/1a/1a250499768a91e3e225a05d141e42d7ed89168ba82c5560777f64b8b29fac4a.png)\n\nLet $C(-1,3)$ and $D(1,-2).$ Find $|\\overset{\\to }{CD}|.$" :question/worked-solution "We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OC}=c=-i+3j, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OD}=d=i-2j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{CD}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CD} & =\\overset{\\to }{OD}-\\overset{\\to }{OC} \\\\  & =d-c \\\\  & =(i-2j)-(-i+3j) \\\\  & =2i-5j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{CD}| & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233598 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c14ed0ed-41e3-5534-b77e-503efe93d887" :question/math-academy-id "q-18055" :question/problem "![](images/1e/1e3e9c336bf85cf0f19b2326f12c5fd986fee5b0aae65b8d79257ea234efee13.png)\n\nPoints $P$ and $Q$ are shown in the picture above. Find $|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}|.$" :question/worked-solution "From the picture, we obtain $P(1,1)$ and $Q(2,3).$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OP}=p=i+j, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OQ}=q=2i+3j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =q-p \\\\  & =(2i+3j)-(i+j) \\\\  & =i+2j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501385 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0445042e-54ee-545e-a3f8-732df318f4f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501380} {:answer/id #uuid "0490c650-33f4-5c2c-b521-fe9b1e566ec1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501381} {:answer/id #uuid "6ddf7c05-e687-5019-8cfe-0f4da5991c7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501395} {:answer/id #uuid "8a0025cb-b64b-5f84-97d4-564a7a574582" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15 \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501397} {:answer/id #uuid "c88fd2c8-d986-5a88-8aac-ff25f7704891" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0490c650-33f4-5c2c-b521-fe9b1e566ec1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501381} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c461d70-6214-536b-9b0f-2806ac3e820b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501386}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "351db615-bec0-5fbb-9adf-d33132b902d9" :question/problem "![](images/07/07a59129f6186959fa9ebad8b924177a81910a3d25c2f292169c41474df99a31.png)\n\nLet $A(-12, 3)$ and $B(9, 0)$. Find $|\\overrightarrow{AB}|$." :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OA} &= a = - 12 i + 3 j, \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{OB} &= b = 9 i.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{AB} &= \\overrightarrow{OB} - \\overrightarrow{OA} \\\\\n&= b - a \\\\\n&= (9 i) - (- 12 i + 3 j) \\\\\n&= 21 i - 3 j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\overrightarrow{AB}| &= \\sqrt{(21)^{2} + (-3)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{441 + 9} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{450} \\\\\n&= 15 \\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501390 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1064156b-f30e-55b2-b6f0-e825bc55e1e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501382} {:answer/id #uuid "22689487-5be7-57f4-83d8-1de65d9b4694" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501384} {:answer/id #uuid "643ef294-255a-50c2-b361-7fb11bf24717" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501393} {:answer/id #uuid "c82c134e-3f2c-5916-9411-d5e7b2847411" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501404} {:answer/id #uuid "f609e524-19c0-530c-a969-08f856f8f9e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10 \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501410}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c82c134e-3f2c-5916-9411-d5e7b2847411" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501404} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3672b93-4679-5491-bb12-4ccb62ec0b4e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501400}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "51236f62-ba5d-5c78-8128-0c42c6d77d9b" :question/problem "![](images/56/5682cc802577e4dd43f42e03bfc829658fc96ca83a15422aa079fe2b43258a0c.png)\n\nLet $A(-8, 2)$ and $B(6, 0)$. Find $|\\overrightarrow{AB}|$." :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OA} &= a = - 8 i + 2 j, \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{OB} &= b = 6 i.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{AB} &= \\overrightarrow{OB} - \\overrightarrow{OA} \\\\\n&= b - a \\\\\n&= (6 i) - (- 8 i + 2 j) \\\\\n&= 14 i - 2 j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\overrightarrow{AB}| &= \\sqrt{(14)^{2} + (-2)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{196 + 4} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{200} \\\\\n&= 10 \\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501391 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4555636f-851f-5e9a-97d4-f0c927f479bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/ma