d}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501407 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70508e9b-a14a-5a98-8e92-1e7ad5d853c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501396} {:answer/id #uuid "8d049bb8-f5e4-5c04-829f-a53cafde9397" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501398} {:answer/id #uuid "a0451aba-8b5c-5281-ac81-2b22e276ad68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501399} {:answer/id #uuid "df4172c0-8628-54c0-81a3-e9013141b07a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501409} {:answer/id #uuid "f95e5d75-a09f-5293-b330-062df6b3f507" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{23}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501412}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df4172c0-8628-54c0-81a3-e9013141b07a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501409} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d4df1b5-ef4c-5db5-95a8-06e66305be52" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501387}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d8e7cd39-a979-5900-aba6-00ca0310cc42" :question/problem "![](images/d7/d7b3f6503172aeab9c4554ffac492a9aab8c16e9ce14f5c552cd1d89dcaa3c66.png)\n\nLet $P(-4, 4)$ and $Q(6, 6)$. Find $|\\overrightarrow{PQ}|$." :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OP} &= p = - 4 i + 4 j, \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{OQ} &= q = 6 i + 6 j.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{PQ} &= \\overrightarrow{OQ} - \\overrightarrow{OP} \\\\\n&= q - p \\\\\n&= (6 i + 6 j) - (- 4 i + 4 j) \\\\\n&= 10 i + 2 j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\overrightarrow{PQ}| &= \\sqrt{(10)^{2} + (2)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{100 + 4} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{104} \\\\\n&= 2 \\sqrt{26}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501414 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1da9c0a6-14cc-517f-a698-c8a70ee46bb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9 \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501383} {:answer/id #uuid "45e58fef-c1c7-52df-807b-c1a8f907804d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501389} {:answer/id #uuid "5bdee396-6d9f-5bbe-8378-a50d04de0635" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501392} {:answer/id #uuid "df2d382e-5a80-52bc-a649-14e4acf7e481" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 \\sqrt{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501408} {:answer/id #uuid "fd3387cd-5801-5797-af72-00603e84116c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 \\sqrt{23}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df2d382e-5a80-52bc-a649-14e4acf7e481" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 \\sqrt{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501408} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7666596-5028-5069-996f-ad5e72c1af9c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501402}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ff8c4899-ff23-5168-90d9-e8d647d7f269" :question/problem "![](images/6b/6bd80d88ece15997923e5860ff1328dea542c2950c9e4399eba6a5e872070f18.png)\n\nLet $P(-6, 6)$ and $Q(9, 9)$. Find $|\\overrightarrow{PQ}|$." :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OP} &= p = - 6 i + 6 j, \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{OQ} &= q = 9 i + 9 j.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{PQ} &= \\overrightarrow{OQ} - \\overrightarrow{OP} \\\\\n&= q - p \\\\\n&= (9 i + 9 j) - (- 6 i + 6 j) \\\\\n&= 15 i + 3 j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\overrightarrow{PQ}| &= \\sqrt{(15)^{2} + (3)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{225 + 9} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{234} \\\\\n&= 3 \\sqrt{26}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector From Position Vectors and then Computing its Magnitude"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087696 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087503 :question/id #uuid "bcb710d0-a687-5686-ae3a-0d0773857530" :question/math-academy-id "e-4391" :question/problem "Which of the following are square matrices?\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "- $U$ is *not* a square matrix since the numbers of rows and columns are not the same. It has $2$ rows and $3$ columns, so it's a $2 \\times 3$ matrix.\n\n- $W$ is a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. It has $3$ rows and $3$ columns, so it is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix.\n\n- $Z$ is a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. It has $2$ rows and $2$ columns, so it is a $2 \\times 2$ matrix.\n\nTherefore, $W$ and $Z$ are square matrices."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ca13445-0218-5950-967e-a68bcfec32c7" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087984 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be125519-2f34-546c-b7bd-23c5ac96496b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459407} {:answer/id #uuid "8cc35c2d-cdfb-54b0-b59a-1ab2c16f4527" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459408}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8cc35c2d-cdfb-54b0-b59a-1ab2c16f4527" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459408} :answer-field